{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_devtools_tap_protocol", "label": "DevTools-Tap-Protokoll", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ein gemultiplexter WebSocket plus ein paar JSON-Endpunkte fuer alle Panels: ein Browser-Tab haelt genau eine Verbindung, ein Panel-Wechsel kostet keinen Reconnect, ein untaetiger Tab kostet nichts. Stabil genug, um einen eigenen Client dagegen zu schreiben."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_protocol_versioning_rule", "label": "Versionierungsregel", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Additive Aenderungen behalten die Version und Clients muessen Unbekanntes ignorieren; alles andere erhoeht sie. Eine Abweichung schliesst den Socket mit 4400, weil ein UI-Bundle, das einen halb verstandenen Actor-Baum rendert, schlimmer ist als ein Banner, das zum Neubauen auffordert."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_handshake", "label": "Handshake (hello / welcome)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Der Client sendet zuerst hello; davor wird nichts akzeptiert. welcome traegt Protokoll- und Serverversion, Systemname, startedAtMs sowie streams und panels als Capability-Ankuendigung \u2014 ein Panel ist active, disabled oder unavailable mit Begruendung."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_client_frames", "label": "Client-Frames", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "hello, subscribe, unsubscribe, request."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_server_frames", "label": "Server-Frames", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "welcome, event, response und error. Ein Fehler mit requestId lehnt diesen Request ab, einer ohne gilt fuer die Verbindung."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_streams", "label": "Tap-Streams", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "stats, actors, cluster, mailboxes, spans, explain und profiler. Ein Abo liefert erst einen Snapshot, dann Deltas \u2014 der Snapshot entsteht auf derselben Mailbox, die die Deltas publiziert, kann also nie aus einer halb aktualisierten Sicht stammen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_sequence_numbers_and_gaps", "label": "Sequenznummern und Luecken", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eine Luecke heisst, Frames wurden verworfen und der inkrementelle Zustand ist geraten \u2014 die UI abonniert dann neu fuer einen frischen Snapshot, statt einen Baum zu zeigen, der still von der Realitaet abweicht."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_cumulative_counters_wire_rule", "label": "Zaehler sind kumulativ, nie Deltas", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Der Client berechnet Raten aus aufeinanderfolgenden Samples, sodass ein Reconnect oder ein verpasster Tick die Zahlen nicht verfaelschen kann."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_requests", "label": "Tap-Requests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pull-Operationen, benannt nach ihrem Panel: explain.*, journal.*, replay.*, profiler.*, stats.history, tracing.buffer. Sie werden ausserhalb der Mailbox des Taps beantwortet, damit ein langsamer Journal-Read keine anderen Tabs blockiert; eine Methode ohne Handler antwortet mit unavailable."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_endpoints", "label": "Tap-Endpunkte", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GET / (UI-Shell), GET /assets/*, GET /api/info (Handshake-Daten als reines JSON, curl-bar) und WS /api/ws."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_decodeclientframe", "label": "decodeClientFrame", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Der Server lehnt alles ab, was kein wohlgeformtes Frame ist, inklusive unbekannter Kinds: die Ignoriere-was-du-nicht-kennst-Haelfte gilt fuer Clients, die Server-Frames lesen \u2014 der Server hat keinen Grund, Frames eines neueren Clients zu akzeptieren."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_devtools_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_handshake", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_devtools_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_client_frames", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_devtools_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_server_frames", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_devtools_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_streams", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_devtools_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_requests", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_devtools_protocol_devtools_tap_protocol", 